{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-125872-r4630104","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Charoset (Maghrebi)","sourcePageId":125872,"sourceRevision":"4630104","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T10:34:09Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Charoset%20(Maghrebi)&oldid=4630104","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:17.827Z","sourceCategories":["Category:African recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for charoset","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using apricot","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using orange juice","Category:Recipes using peach","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegan recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f4eeac4440ddd07e629beca58eb62b7d4fe34c178532374d4e3f35d504f4e023","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Passover recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Maghrebi charoset''' is a variety of [[Cookbook:Charoset|charoset]] served during the Jewish celebration of Passover by Jews from Northwest Africa. Serve as part of the [[Cookbook:Seder|seder]]. The northwest African tradition uses bitter greens such as endive rather than horseradish with the Charoseth.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white [[cookbook:raisin|raisins]]\n* ½ cup dried [[cookbook:apricot|apricots]] or dried [[cookbook:peach|peaches]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 [[cookbook:orange|oranges]], juiced\n* ¼ cup chopped [[cookbook:almond|almonds]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 1 tsp [[cookbook:ginger|ginger]], preferably freshly-grated\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[cookbook:honey|honey]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Matzo Meal|matsoh meal]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Soak dried fruit in juice until plumped.\n# Mash reconstituted fruit with almond and spices to get a mortar-like texture.\n# Adjust texture with matsoh meal and if needed, sweeten with honey.\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for charoset]]\n[[Category:African recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apricot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using peach]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Charoset (Maghrebi)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ cup white raisins","sourceText":"1½ cup white raisins","amountText":"1½ cup white raisins","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup dried apricots or dried peaches, chopped","sourceText":"½ cup dried apricots or dried peaches, chopped","amountText":"½ cup dried apricots or dried peaches, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 oranges, juiced","sourceText":"2 oranges, juiced","amountText":"2 oranges, juiced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"¼ cup chopped almonds","sourceText":"¼ cup chopped almonds","amountText":